Z||000000||Gary W||11-21-2001||10:25 PM||||Just installed Rodney's Muncie select arm rebuild kit, along with a sport shifter. The difference the rebuild kit made is UNBELIEVABLE. This on a car with only 38k on it. It's still notchy, but ALL the slop is gone. Just 2 little bushings...Great stuff, Rodney.<P>Too bad I busted a sail panel putting it in. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000001||TylerB11||11-22-2001||12:06 AM||||I know! Mine was very sloppy..the bushings made it better, but it still wasn't good? know why? the shifter arm (the one the selector moves up and down) had broken at the weld! no matter, brought it to a welding shop and they fixed it for 2 bucks. Now its real tight, no slop. Still notchy, but those bushings were the best bang per buck of any upgrades I've made so far.<P>||||reg||1
